    {"on": "I have never heard one word of insult or unkindness from you", "text": "The last private voice in the Iliad is Helen's, praising Hector not for his courage but for his kindness. Of all the things that could be said of the greatest Trojan, the poem ends with this: he was gentle to a woman everyone else blamed."},
